        "original_id": "0a047b03-15c5-5029-a46d-78d87b4ed032",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bob Beers, Harry Reid\n- Events: 2006 Nevada Republican gubernatorial nomination, 2016 United States Senate election in Nevada\n- Places: Nevada\n- Topics: Republican and Democratic candidacies, election timing\n\nFacts:\n- Bob Beers ran unsuccessfully for the Republican nomination for Governor of Nevada in 2006.\n- In January 2014, Bob Beers announced that he would run against Democratic Senator Harry Reid in the 2016 United States Senate election in Nevada.\n- In June 2015, Bob Beers withdrew from the 2016 United States Senate race in Nevada.\n- The 2016 United States Senate election in Nevada was held on November 8, 2016.\n- The 2016 United States Senate election in Nevada elected a member of the United States Senate to represent Nevada.\n- The 2016 United States Senate election in Nevada was held concurrently with the 2016 United States presidential election, other United States Senate elections, United States House elections, and various state and local elections.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
